class.description:
[CgameFFTOcean] generates a tileable ocean height grid with the method of Jerry Tessendorf, "Simulating Ocean Water" (2001). A Phillips spectrum [code]h0(k)[/code] is built once from a seed by [method setup]. Each call to [method evaluate] computes [code]h(k, t) = h0(k) e^(i w t) + conj(h0(-k)) e^(-i w t)[/code] with the deep-water dispersion [code]w = sqrt(g |k|)[/code] and transforms it with an inverse 2D radix-2 FFT into a real height grid. The grid can be sampled on the CPU (for example for buoyancy, see [method sample_height]) or uploaded as a texture for vertex displacement (see [method displacement_image]).
The rows and columns of the 2D transform are independent and run on the [WorkerThreadPool]; the result is bit-identical to a serial run. The spectrum is built serially from [RandomNumberGenerator] so the same seed always produces the same ocean.
This class is the native counterpart of the GDScript [code]fft_ocean.gd[/code].
[codeblock]
var ocean := CgameFFTOcean.new()
ocean.setup(64, 200.0, Vector2(12.0, 5.0), 4.0, 1234)
func _process(_delta):
    var heights: PackedFloat32Array = ocean.evaluate(Time.get_ticks_msec() / 1000.0)
    var height_here := ocean.sample_height(heights, Vector2(10.0, 20.0))
[/codeblock]
